      "reason": "The complete unit is on printed 90/PDF128. 'That Son of Man' fits the selected wording; printed note 18 records variation in its ordering. The second clause continues the naming statement elliptically. 'His name was before' risks introducing a separate assertion of existence rather than making that ellipsis clear. The printed asterisk before the Son-of-Man expression is editorial, not a source word.",
      "suggested_text": "At that hour that Son of Man was named in the presence of the Lord of Spirits, and his name was named before the Head of Days.",
